From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] give the priorities table the full page width

0063 tightened the table and it was still cramped, because the constraint is
not in the table -- it is in the wrapper. `SettingsFieldSection` is a
`lg:grid-cols-8` layout that spends 2 columns on the label and leaves 6 for its
slot. That is right for a toggle or a single input, and wrong for a five-column
table: it capped the table at 75% of the page and forced the channel chips to
wrap however narrow the remainder got.

The section is replaced with a plain full-width block and the label moved above
the table, so the table gets the whole content width. Every other section on
the page keeps the two-column layout -- this is the one that needed to differ,
and the comment says why so nobody "restores consistency" later.

The editor renders its own explanatory paragraph, so the section's `help-text`
is dropped rather than duplicated above it. `SettingsFieldSection` is still
imported and used by the other sections on this page.

Real `git diff` against the component as extracted from the patched image.
diff --git a/app/javascript/dashboard/routes/dashboard/settings/inbox/settingsPage/CollaboratorsPage.vue b/app/javascript/dashboard/routes/dashboard/settings/inbox/settingsPage/CollaboratorsPage.vue
index c38e69f..f5c46a6 100644
--- a/app/javascript/dashboard/routes/dashboard/settings/inbox/settingsPage/CollaboratorsPage.vue
+++ b/app/javascript/dashboard/routes/dashboard/settings/inbox/settingsPage/CollaboratorsPage.vue
@@ -662,13 +662,21 @@ onMounted(() => {
       </SettingsToggleSection>
     </SettingsAccordion>
 
-    <SettingsFieldSection
-      label="Agent Channel Priorities"
-      help-text="Set each agent's primary channel and any additional channels they handle."
-      class="[&>div]:!items-start"
-    >
-      <AgentPrioritiesEditor />
-    </SettingsFieldSection>
+    <!-- Full width on purpose, unlike every other section on this page.
+         SettingsFieldSection is a lg:grid-cols-8 layout that spends 2 columns
+         on the label and leaves 6 for the slot -- fine for a toggle or a single
+         input, but it squeezed this table into 75% of the page and forced the
+         five channel chips to wrap. The label moves above the table so the
+         table gets the whole width. The editor renders its own explanatory
+         paragraph, so the section's help-text is not duplicated here. -->
+    <div class="w-full py-2 mb-2">
+      <label class="text-heading-3 text-n-slate-12">
+        Agent Channel Priorities
+      </label>
+      <div class="mt-2">
+        <AgentPrioritiesEditor />
+      </div>
+    </div>
 
     <woot-modal
       v-if="showDeleteConfirmModal"
